<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maeda Toshinaga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1562">1562</a>–<a href="/years/1614">1614</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maeda Toshinaga was a Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a>, eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maeda-toshiie">Maeda Toshiie</a> and second lord of the Kaga domain. After his father's death in 1599 he submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-ieyasu">Tokugawa Ieyasu</a> and fought on his side in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-sekigahara">Sekigahara</a> campaign of 1600. He was rewarded with lands in Kaga, Noto and Etchu, making the Maeda the wealthiest daimyo family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maeda-toshinaga.jpg" alt="Maeda Toshinaga" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknow person · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%89%8D%E7%94%B0_%E5%88%A9%E9%95%B7,.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
